halogen: NOTE this server now holds most of the machine, and 308 contiguous 2 MiB blocks remain. It runs best on a host of its own. If other large processes share this machine they will compete for what is left, and when it runs out BOTH they and this server can stall for minutes at a time at full CPU with no disk activity and no output, which is not a crash and needs no restart. Lowering HALOGEN_KV_POOL_POSITIONS gives some back. HALOGEN_FLASH_PIN_TRUNK=0 gives a great deal back and costs several times the decode speed, so it is a last resort.
